From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mafien0
Date: Thu Jul 16 2026
Subject: [PATCH 9/8] Fix xdg-decoration configure not making window visible

xdgSurfaceHandleConfigure checks window->wl.xdg.decorationMode before
making the window visible, but the xdg-decoration configure event may
arrive *after* the xdg-surface configure event. In that case
decorationMode is still 0 when xdgSurfaceHandleConfigure runs, so
window->wl.visible is never set.

This causes eglSwapBuffers to be skipped (swapBuffersEGL checks
window->wl.visible) and the window is never presented to the compositor.

Fix by also setting window->wl.visible in xdgDecorationHandleConfigure
once the decoration mode is known.

diff --git a/src/wl_window.c b/src/wl_window.c
index 1234567..abcdef0 100644
--- a/src/wl_window.c
+++ b/src/wl_window.c
@@ -444,7 +444,7 @@ static void xdgDecorationHandleConfigure(void* userData,
     _GLFWwindow* window = userData;

     window->wl.xdg.decorationMode = mode;
-
+
     if (mode == ZXDG_TOPLEVEL_DECORATION_V1_MODE_CLIENT_SIDE)
     {
         if (window->decorated && !window->monitor)
@@ -452,6 +452,12 @@ static void xdgDecorationHandleConfigure(void* userData,
     }
     else
         destroyFallbackDecorations(window);
+
+    if (!window->wl.visible)
+    {
+        window->wl.visible = GLFW_TRUE;
+        _glfwInputWindowDamage(window);
+    }
 }
